{"id":"45","title":"Work and Study","goal":"Recognize selected job, education and employment terms and use them to describe a situation or ask a question.","language":"en","study":[{"id":"45-study-0","title":"Start here","blocks":[{"id":"ch45-b0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Choose the words relevant to your work or study. These groups support Chapters 46–55; you do not need to memorize every occupation before starting an interaction."}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":6,"ja":"","theme":"work-vocabulary"},{"id":"45-study-1","title":"People and jobs","blocks":[{"id":"ch45-b1","type":"table","header":[[{"text":"Word"}],[{"text":"Meaning"}]],"rows":[[[{"text":"server / chef"}],[{"text":"a person serving food / a professional cook"}]],[[{"text":"receptionist"}],[{"text":"a person welcoming visitors or handling incoming requests"}]],[[{"text":"teacher / librarian"}],[{"text":"a person teaching / a person working professionally with library services"}]],[[{"text":"doctor"}],[{"text":"in healthcare, a medical professional who evaluates and treats illness"}]],[[{"text":"nurse"}],[{"text":"a healthcare professional providing and coordinating patient care"}]],[[{"text":"pharmacist"}],[{"text":"a professional dispensing medicines and explaining their use"}]],[[{"text":"mechanic"}],[{"text":"a person repairing machines, often vehicles"}]],[[{"text":"electrician / plumber"}],[{"text":"workers specializing in electrical systems / pipes and water systems"}]],[[{"text":"accountant"}],[{"text":"a person working with financial records and accounts"}]],[[{"text":"engineer / architect"}],[{"text":"a professional designing technical systems / buildings"}]],[[{"text":"real estate agent"}],[{"text":"a person helping with property transactions"}]],[[{"text":"freelancer"}],[{"text":"someone taking work independently from clients"}]]],"span":[10,23],"phraseIds":["ch45-p77905302010782","ch45-p80561474911152","ch45-p253777885198718","ch45-p1675578861164","ch45-p62584026500665","ch45-p66181225063564","ch45-p191595355876915","ch45-p219479458712684","ch45-p193513517312731","ch45-p177362590662210","ch45-p54857210237619","ch45-p5387005485392"],"phraseCells":[["ch45-p77905302010782",null],["ch45-p80561474911152",null],["ch45-p253777885198718",null],["ch45-p1675578861164",null],["ch45-p62584026500665",null],["ch45-p66181225063564",null],["ch45-p191595355876915",null],["ch45-p219479458712684",null],["ch45-p193513517312731",null],["ch45-p177362590662210",null],["ch45-p54857210237619",null],["ch45-p5387005485392",null]]},{"id":"ch45-b2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Other useful jobs include "},{"text":"lawyer","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"dentist","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"veterinarian","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"flight attendant","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"courier","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"security guard","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"firefighter","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"app developer","emphasis":true},{"text":", and "},{"text":"childcare provider","emphasis":true},{"text":". Say "},{"text":"I work as a receptionist","emphasis":true},{"text":" or "},{"text":"I'm studying engineering","emphasis":true},{"text":" to describe a role or subject."}],"span":[25,25],"phraseIds":["ch45-p253982959213149","ch45-p267903443726989","ch45-p271271254815538","ch45-p43423492059995","ch45-p93598095645807","ch45-p218827521426331","ch45-p158280792485925","ch45-p79411012054536","ch45-p36063659563709","ch45-p154619811624212","ch45-p86246079805106"]}],"line":8,"ja":"","theme":"work-vocabulary"},{"id":"45-study-2","title":"Education","blocks":[{"id":"ch45-b3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"class","emphasis":true},{"text":" can be a teaching session or the students attending it. A "},{"text":"course","emphasis":true},{"text":" covers a subject through organized study. A "},{"text":"lecture","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a talk used to teach or explain a subject. "},{"text":"Homework","emphasis":true},{"text":" is study work assigned outside class; an "},{"text":"assignment","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a particular task. An "},{"text":"exam","emphasis":true},{"text":" or "},{"text":"test","emphasis":true},{"text":" assesses learning. "},{"text":"Pass","emphasis":true},{"text":" means meet its stated standard; "},{"text":"fail","emphasis":true},{"text":" means not meet it."}],"span":[29,29],"phraseIds":["ch45-p200110787337508","ch45-p148261391504734","ch45-p105417782013207","ch45-p179949021177340","ch45-p57652200297802","ch45-p244873609073501","ch45-p92931499462901","ch45-p149732790355740","ch45-p76787600747602"]},{"id":"ch45-b4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"degree","emphasis":true},{"text":" is an academic qualification awarded after a college or university program. A "},{"text":"diploma","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a document showing completion of study; some programs also use the word as a qualification name. A "},{"text":"certificate","emphasis":true},{"text":" documents completion or a particular achievement; ask what a course's certificate represents. The names alone do not establish that qualifications are equivalent. "},{"text":"Graduation","emphasis":true},{"text":" is completing a course of study or the related ceremony. A "},{"text":"schedule","emphasis":true},{"text":" shows planned times. "},{"text":"Tuition","emphasis":true},{"text":" refers to the charge for instruction in the education context used here."}],"span":[31,31],"phraseIds":["ch45-p142743930721548","ch45-p34093772606589","ch45-p131047642525995","ch45-p169708911749981","ch45-p14635260671521","ch45-p174325474919534"]}],"line":27,"ja":"","theme":"work-vocabulary"},{"id":"45-study-3","title":"Employment","blocks":[{"id":"ch45-b5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"An "},{"text":"employer","emphasis":true},{"text":" hires people; an "},{"text":"employee","emphasis":true},{"text":" works for the employer. "},{"text":"Full-time","emphasis":true},{"text":" and "},{"text":"part-time","emphasis":true},{"text":" describe working arrangements; ask what hours a particular job involves. "},{"text":"Temporary","emphasis":true},{"text":" work has a limited expected period; "},{"text":"permanent","emphasis":true},{"text":" describes an ongoing arrangement, not a guarantee of lifetime employment."}],"span":[35,35],"phraseIds":["ch45-p123870967102477","ch45-p201849054505662","ch45-p188536418930579","ch45-p7146195843399","ch45-p178461361736934","ch45-p108121869575077"]},{"id":"ch45-b6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"shift","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a scheduled period of work. "},{"text":"Overtime","emphasis":true},{"text":" is work beyond a relevant usual or defined period. "},{"text":"Wages","emphasis":true},{"text":" means pay earned for work, often discussed by the hour. A "},{"text":"salary","emphasis":true},{"text":" is an agreed regular amount of pay, often stated as a yearly figure. "},{"text":"Hourly pay","emphasis":true},{"text":" states payment by the hour. A job offer explains how that job's pay is calculated. A "},{"text":"pay stub","emphasis":true},{"text":" lists earnings and deductions. "},{"text":"Benefits","emphasis":true},{"text":" are employment offerings beyond ordinary pay. "},{"text":"Paid time off","emphasis":true},{"text":" names time away for which pay is provided under the employer's arrangements. "},{"text":"Resign","emphasis":true},{"text":" means leave a job by your own decision; "},{"text":"retire","emphasis":true},{"text":" means stop working as a later-life or career decision."}],"span":[37,37],"phraseIds":["ch45-p164962805340848","ch45-p225261365825100","ch45-p172850182306403","ch45-p43112047817943","ch45-p97955383980432","ch45-p45542655576982","ch45-p61271768396408","ch45-p11312102089828","ch45-p99533762710650","ch45-p58604417703509"]}],"line":33,"ja":"","theme":"work-vocabulary"},{"id":"45-words","title":"Words & phrases","blocks":[{"id":"45-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch45-v0","ch45-v1","ch45-v2","ch45-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"45-practice-0","title":"Take your turn","blocks":[{"id":"ch45-b7","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"Choose four terms that match your interests. Define each in your own words."}],"id":"ch45-b7-0"},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"Identify the words: the hiring organization; a planned work period; a charge for a course; a record of earnings."}],"id":"ch45-b7-1"},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"Use this fictional role: part-time receptionist, studying accounting, Tuesday classes. Say two sentences, then ask about the job's hours."}],"id":"ch45-b7-2"}],"span":[41,43]}],"line":41,"ja":"","theme":"work-vocabulary","answers":[{"id":"ch45-b8","type":"answer","runs":[{"text":"Sample possibilities:","emphasis":true},{"text":" "},{"text":"Employer, shift, tuition, pay stub.","emphasis":true},{"text":" “I work part-time as a receptionist. I'm studying accounting, with classes on Tuesdays. What hours does the job involve?”"}],"span":[45,45]},{"id":"ch45-b9","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Cover the lists later and retrieve only your chosen words. Check that you can distinguish the people, activity, qualification and work condition instead of treating related terms as identical."}],"span":[47,47]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch45-p1341189905","en":"server","section":"45-study-1","context":"a person serving food / a professional cook","kind":"word","studyId":"ch45-p77905302010782"},{"id":"ch45-p4124749714","en":"chef","section":"45-study-1","context":"a person serving food / a professional cook","kind":"word","studyId":"ch45-p77905302010782"},{"art":"word-reception.svg","id":"ch45-p80561474911152","en":"receptionist","section":"45-study-1","context":"The person who welcomes visitors and handles appointments or inquiries.","kind":"word","studyId":"ch45-p80561474911152"},{"id":"ch45-p1612136853","en":"teacher","section":"45-study-1","context":"